TITLE:: SPLog
summary:: what happened on the server, a line each, bursts as one line
categories:: Libraries>ServerPanel
related:: Classes/SPTree, Classes/SPSnapshot

DESCRIPTION::
link::Classes/SPTree::'s log: every node that started, ended, was paused or resumed, every FAILURE the server sent, every problem that came and went, every snapshot, each with its time. As rows, entries of one kind, SynthDef and place that follow each other less than link::#*burstTime:: apart are one row with a count, for link::#*burstSpan:: seconds at most: a pattern's events read as a line every few seconds. Language only; it keeps the last link::#*maxEntries::.

code::
l = SPLog.new;
l.add(\born, (id: 1001, def: \mine, pathText: "default group"));
l.add(\born, (id: 1002, def: \mine, pathText: "default group"));
l.rows.do { |r| SPLog.lineOf(r).postln };
l.text.postln;
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
An empty log.

METHOD:: maxEntries
How many entries are kept: 3000.

METHOD:: burstTime
The most seconds between two entries of one burst: 1.

METHOD:: burstSpan
The most seconds a burst row covers: 15.

METHOD:: lineOf
An entry, or a burst row, as a line of text without the time.
ARGUMENT:: e
An entry.

METHOD:: clock
An elapsed time on the wall clock: code::"14:03:22.5"::.
ARGUMENT:: time
A time as code::Main.elapsedTime:: counts.

METHOD:: what
The first word of an entry's line: started, ended, paused ...
ARGUMENT:: e
An entry.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: add
Add an entry.
ARGUMENT:: kind
code::\born \ended \paused \resumed \fail \problem \cleared \snapshot \note::.
ARGUMENT:: more
An Event of whatever else is known: code::id::, code::def::, code::pathText::, code::parent::, code::lived::, code::text::.
RETURNS:: the entry

METHOD:: rows
The entries as rows, newest first.
ARGUMENT:: bursts
Whether bursts are one row.
ARGUMENT:: filter
Only the lines that contain this.

METHOD:: text
The whole log as text, oldest first, a line an entry.

METHOD:: entries
The entries, oldest first.

METHOD:: since
The entries from a time on.
ARGUMENT:: time
A time as code::Main.elapsedTime:: counts.

METHOD:: size
How many entries.

METHOD:: clear
Forget them.

METHOD:: onAdd
A function called with every entry as it is added.

METHOD:: startedAt
When the log was made.
